=======================================================================
 test_createpts - the createpts command (point distributions)
=======================================================================

WHAT THIS IS

  Tests of LaGriT's createpts, the options most used first:

      createpts / xyz | rtz | rtp / ni,nj,nk / mins / maxs / iiz,ijz,ikz
                [ / irat,jrat,krat / rx,ry,rz ]
      createpts / line / n / / / start / end / iz ...
      createpts / brick / xyz | rtz / ...            (vertices + hexes)

  Each deck makes vertices, dumps them, and (where they span a volume or
  a plane) connects them into a mesh: tets for 3D sets (filter, rmpoint
  / compress, connect), triangles for a planar set (triplane), or the
  brick's own hexes and quads. The checker compares the vertices with
  where the DOCUMENTATION says they go (lanl.github.io/LaGriT, the
  createpts pages), not with a copy of the code.

  Not yet covered (planned, after these have run): sphere, random,
  vector, interp, voronoi, median, amr. poisson_disk has its own suites.

QUICK START

  run_createpts_tests.sh                           about 12 seconds

  then open logs/summary.html.

  Requires: LaGriT, Python 3 (standard library only), a POSIX shell.

